<article class="env-remark" id="0D3G">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0D3G">Remark <span data-tag="0D3G">90.13.5</span>.</a> Let $F : \mathcal{C}_\Lambda \to \textit{Sets}$ be a predeformation functor satisfying (S1) and (S2). The condition $\dim _ k TF < \infty $ is precisely condition (H3) from Schlessinger's paper. Recall that (S1) and (S2) correspond to conditions (H1) and (H2), see Remark <a href="/tag/06HY" data-tag="06HY">90.10.3</a>. Thus Lemma <a href="/tag/06IW" data-tag="06IW">90.13.4</a> tells us </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  (H1) + (H2) + (H3) \Rightarrow \text{ there exists a versal formal object}  \]
</div>
  <p> for predeformation functors. We will make the link with hulls in Remark <a href="/tag/06IY" data-tag="06IY">90.15.6</a>. </p>
</article>